## 🚀 Performance Discussion

A bug-free application can still fail if it runs slowly. Optimizing backend processing speeds keeps our applications highly scalable:

* **The Power of SOQL Bulkification:** Ensure that every query uses highly selective `WHERE` clauses on indexed fields (like `Id`, `Name`, or custom External IDs). Never embed queries inside `for` loops; extract records collectively into Map structures before iterating.
* **Efficient Heap Size Management:** Asynchronous Apex provides a 12MB heap limit, but synchronous blocks restrict memory to 6MB. To avoid running out of memory during large transactions, process data loops using `SOQL For Loops` (e.g., `for (List<Account> accts : [SELECT Id FROM Account])`), which chunks records into sets of 200 rather than loading thousands into memory at once.
* **CPU Time Limit Mitigation:** Reduce complex nested loops ($O(n^2)$ complexity). Utilize Apex Collections (`Map<Id, sObject>`) to quickly relate records in memory using an immediate $O(1)$ lookup algorithm instead of burning system processing seconds.

