## 🧠 Reflection

Day 16 highlighted that debugging is not just a reactive fix—it is an intentional engineering practice. Writing code is only half the battle; knowing exactly how to trace its execution when things go sideways separates an amateur coder from an enterprise-grade developer.

Learning how to navigate execution trees in the Developer Console and parsing unminified JavaScript source files in Browser DevTools completely removes the guesswork from debugging. Moving forward, prioritizing defensive patterns—like bulkifying queries, checking for null values up front, and respecting component lifecycle loops—will drastically reduce the time we spend hunting down errors. This approach helps ensure that the systems we build run efficiently and scale reliably.
